# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots the metasploitable services - smbd with
# `wide links = yes` (symlink traversal out of a share) listening on 139/445 -
# and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * Samba is ALREADY serving when the agent starts, so verify.sh can require a
#     live smbd and read the per-connection effective config;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting smbd cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Note: smbd forks a fresh child per client connection and re-reads smb.conf, so
# a `wide links = no` edit takes effect for the next attacker connection WITHOUT
# a full restart - there is no "forgot to restart" variant. The value of
# preserving the CMD is that a stopped/broken smbd is observably a FAILURE.
